{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful","id":101605,"title":"GMC defense and armour too powerful?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-29T16:57:25-07:00","id":101605,"title":"GMC defense and armour too powerful?","content":"Hi<br /> I've got a question in regards to defense how your expereinces there are and if someone uses a workaround.<br /> <br /> I've had 2 rounds now that got into melee in medieval times. The first time the chars didnt have good stats so I didnt think much there, but this time around they had acceptable stats<br /> with base dicepools of 7-10 for hitting enemies. The problem was the damage that was dealt and that if any of the enemies had armour almost none would have been hurt at all.<br /> <br /> Last round<br /> Attacker: Str 2, melee 1 with spec and a sword. The defender had normal stats and a bit of battle experience 4 defense which reduced the attacking dicepool to 0 (chance roll).<br /> In combination with leather armour eeven with willpower spent almost no damage.<br /> <br /> This round<br /> we had a werewolf who had a base dice pool of 7 and a bite of 1L. the defender had 4 defense so only 3 dices to hit. if the defender had any armour (leather as example) then the<br /> chances to do ANY damage at all would have been almost neglible. Even so the werewolf did almost alyways only 1 damage.<br /> <br /> A demon who had large blades form (4 damage) had way more chance of doing real damage to the enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> So my question is if anyone else ran into the problem that ppl who had only 0-1L attacks were almost effectless in combat (especially with armour) and that<br /> the high gmc defense reduces normal non master combatants (with 3 strength and 3 dots in the skill + speciality) to levels where you need QUITE some luck to be able to hit at all<br /> <br /> and if so what workarounds you use.<br /> <br /> tnx<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T17:18:22-07:00","id":101610,"title":"","content":"If you aren't applying conditions/tilts you may want to try doing that, the combat system also expects you to use Willpower points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T17:19:55-07:00","id":101615,"title":"","content":"Spend Willpower, fish for situational modifiers, get your dice pool as high as possible, and use called shots. If you aim for areas the armor doesn't cover you don't have to worry about the damage reduction, and if you land a good hit on a called shot you can impose tilts which will make subsequent attacks easier to land. The GMC combat rules were intentionally designed to facilitate and encourage this kind of play. That way you're improvising tactical maneuvers to fish for situational bonuses, making called shots to circumvent armor and impose penalties, and actually spending your resources, instead of just rolling back and forth until someone gets enough 8s 9s or 10s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:10:18-07:00","id":101672,"title":"","content":"Just to add and re-iterate on the above:<ul><li>Be generous with Willpower use</li> <li>In a combat-heavy chronicle, consider using Fighting Styles, either as Merits as presented or manoeuvres that are available to everyone</li> <li>If a character will roll a chance die no matter what, take all the penalties you can get. If the character does get the 10 he will inflict a Tilt that is likely going to end the match</li> <li>Aim for unarmoured body parts</li> <li>Consider the environment and use it to your advantage</li> <li>Consider allowing the <i>Aim </i>action to be taken in melee, representing combatants lining up their attacks and waiting for the right moment</li> <li>Consider allowing &quot;social attacks&quot; to gain benefits (like goading someone into an All-out Attack)</li> <li>Consider fatigue in longer fights</li> <li>Do not forget the Defense penalty from heavy armour</li> <li>Do not forget even if armour negates all Lethal Damage, the target still always takes at least one point of Bashing Damage</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 03-29-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:41:32-07:00","id":101693,"title":"","content":"Really from a role-playing perspective any fight that ends in death is a big deal. So perhaps you should view the low damage output in a fair fight as a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:42:17-07:00","id":101712,"title":"","content":"Or simply use Down and Dirty and the optional Beaten Down rules (someone taking lethal surrenders).<br /> <br /> Additionally, consider how specs stack in this setting. Take a character with Strength 3 and Brawl 3... Give him appropriate specialty in say, Urhsul, All Out Attack, Called Shot and bites each with Area of Expertise; that's a +8 to the base of Strength 5 and brawl 3 and 2 from the regular All Out, 18 dice. Toss in something situational such as &quot;packmates&quot; (from hunting like a pack of wolves do) into brawl as well as another specialty and it's a +10 for a base of 20 dice. Even with a -4 from defense, and a -4 from targeting your opponent's hand, you got 12 dice to chew his hand off, giving the opponent further penalties, making him lose his weapon, heck you can inflict it twice. Targeting his leg and accounting for his defense it comes down to -6; That's 14 dice worth of damage, which means you're pretty much guaranteed to eventually fuck his leg up.<br /> <br /> That's just how scary a Rahu should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-29-2014, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:54:26-07:00","id":101720,"title":"","content":"Also with the Beaten Down rules, someone who takes bashing damage &gt; their stamina also surrenders. So even with a heavily-armored character, it will only take a few hits to get them to that point (although, with Werewolves I houserule that it takes lethal &gt; stamina or any agg to make them surrender, because they heal Lethal like humans heal bashing, so I figure they'd treat it as such for the purposes of being Beaten Down).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:59:48-07:00","id":101725,"title":"","content":"Or use things that are more than 1L... That makes a big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T21:28:57-07:00","id":101738,"title":"","content":"These are things to know. It'll make combat a whole lot easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T01:45:43-07:00","id":101824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=101725#post101725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or use things that are more than 1L... That makes a big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really possible with how damage is converted from nwod tot nwod-gmc if I take war form, near wolf or wolf form as examples there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Do not forget the Defense penalty from heavy armour</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>In the first round I had counted it in that is how the enemies of them did get &quot;low&quot; defenses with their leather armour (2 armour, -1 def).<br /> In the second round I took unarmoured opponents sans 1 who had a magical power that granted him 2 armour (he had a base defense of 3 thus it stayed 3 there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, consider how specs stack in this setting. </div> </div> </div>Since when do specs stack? First time I read that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you aren't applying conditions/tilts you may want to try doing that, the combat system also expects you to use Willpower points.<br /> <br /> and<br /> Aim for unarmoured body parts </div> </div> </div>That is why I asked there as with how things went in those 2 combats They needed willpower to even have 1-2 dices to be able to hit at all<br /> without even aiming at unarmoured body parts. If they had aimed at speicifc body parts wthey would have been down to chance dices again.<br /> And tilts /conditions were almost impossible to get with no one able to roll an exceptional<br /> <br /> or am I misunderstanding tehre something about the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 03-30-2014, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T03:34:29-07:00","id":101852,"title":"","content":"Also, take Area of Specialization in a melee/brawl specialization, like Claw or Bite or anything you may want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T04:29:00-07:00","id":101860,"title":"","content":"Quoted for truth:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC pg.150</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Note on Specialties</span><br /> You may only purchase one instance of a given Specialty, although multiple Specialties may apply to a given roll. For example, Surgery and Cardiology may apply to a Medicine roll to perform heart surgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since GMC, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T06:59:10-07:00","id":101901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=101824#post101824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That is why I asked there as with how things went in those 2 combats They needed willpower to even have 1-2 dices to be able to hit at all without even aiming at unarmoured body parts. If they had aimed at speicifc body parts wthey would have been down to chance dices again. And tilts /conditions were almost impossible to get with no one able to roll an exceptional or am I misunderstanding tehre something about the rules?</div> </div> </div> </div> You're not misunderstanding, you're just not being generous enough with situational modifiers as ST. Give your players bonus dice for things like using the environment to their advantage, or using tactics like one distracting the enemy and another attacking them from behind when they're off guard. Besides, all it takes is one good hit to cause a Tilt, and then every following attack will be much easier to land, so consider things like allowing the players to use the teamwork mechanic to all focus their attacks on one point. Encourage the players to use all-out attacks for extra dice when they need them. And maybe most important of all, use the Beaten Down and Surrender rules. A lot of people don't like them because they seem like they'll make fights end too fast. They actually improve combat a lot, I'm convinced the GMC combat rules were written assuming Beaten Down was being used by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:18:04-07:00","id":101939,"title":"","content":"This is how I use it<br /> A) Remove only dexterity , not athletics, on passive defense , only roll dexterity + athletics when dodging .<br /> B) Roll Dexteritry +Atletics as reflexive action , each success removes one from enemy attack . Add 2 on dexterity+athletics when dodging (the opposite of all out attacks)<br /> <br /> In general high armor is rare , is more often to see +3 swords-axes , rather than +3 armors , also armor is damaged , after you pass damage armor prbably takes some damage too .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:24:51-07:00","id":101944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=101939#post101939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I use it A) Remove only dexterity , not athletics, on passive defense , only roll dexterity + athletics when dodging . B) Roll Dexteritry +Atletics as reflexive action , each success removes one from enemy attack . Add 2 on dexterity+athletics when dodging (the opposite of all out attacks) In general high armor is rare , is more often to see +3 swords-axes , rather than +3 armors , also armor is damaged , after you pass damage armor prbably takes some damage too .</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm I like the idea of armor taking damage . Do you have a system for how you calculate the damage dealt to the armor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:57:40-07:00","id":102419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=101944#post101944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm I like the idea of armor taking damage . Do you have a system for how you calculate the damage dealt to the armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Example : A character takes 5 lethal damage from a shot and has 1/2 armor , he will take 2 bashing and 2 lethal , since the attack passed the armor with lethal damage , the 1 lethal that has been soaked does 1 structure damage to the armor . This only applies when lethal damage pierces the armor , bashing is not calculated . If the attack did not pass the armor with lethal then the armor takes no damage . If the armor takes damage equal to it's durability then is not functional but fixable , at half structure point damage it gives penalty on crafts rolls and more money are needed to fix it.<br /> <br /> The same principle goes for weapons as well , when you damage an item with a weapon there is a chance for the weapon to take structure damage , or if your attack is too strong and you bring more successes than the weapon's durability it takes structure damage as well for every point of damage done above it's durability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 03-31-2014, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:00:59-07:00","id":102734,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=101901#post101901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're not misunderstanding, you're just not being generous enough with situational modifiers as ST. Give your players bonus dice for things like using the environment to their advantage, or using tactics like one distracting the enemy and another attacking them from behind when they're off guard. Besides, all it takes is one good hit to cause a Tilt, and then every following attack will be much easier to land, so consider things like allowing the players to use the teamwork mechanic to all focus their attacks on one point. Encourage the players to use all-out attacks for extra dice when they need them. And maybe most important of all, use the Beaten Down and Surrender rules. A lot of people don't like them because they seem like they'll make fights end too fast. They actually improve combat a lot, I'm convinced the GMC combat rules were written assuming Beaten Down was being used by default.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">hmmmm in the cases I had environment was not possible (medieval setting, they entered a side alley and found two unconscious or dead peasants and 3 cloaked adversaries and attacked them. At max there had been a barrell or something similar in there. Additionally it was night, although in meelee I didnt rule that in [forgot about it but even so both sides would have had the same mali there]).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In total it was 4 players against 3 npc.</span></span></span><br /> Strongest 2 players were a werewolf and a demon (7 defense each with the werewolf in urshul form thus bite+2L the demon had a 4L weaponry form).<br /> Next strongest player hd 7 dices with a knife and tried to sneak upon the enemies in the darkness but failed his stealth roll (9 dices with 0 succs). he had 5 defense<br /> <br /> The NPCs had<br /> 2x 4 defense, 0 armour with 4 attack dice (2 dex, 2 skill), swords<br /> 1x 3 defense, 2 armour (supernatural power) with 6 attack dice (4 dex, 2 skill), claws (1L)<br /> <br /> the two lower npc ganged up on the werewolf after round 1, and the stronger enemy hit the 3rd strongest and the 4th player (only 1 hit landed on the 3rd strongest player).<br /> <br /> the npc were down to chance dices (except the 2nd one who ganged up and the stronger one), and the players usually were down to chance rolls except against the stronger npc.<br /> <br /> The strongest 2 ganged up on one of the weaker npc and the other two on the stronger npc and like I said 2 npc ganged up on the werewolf beginning with the 2nd round.<br /> <br /> Combat as in total 4-5 rounds long.<br /> <br /> <br /> The result was quite a few non hits / non damage hits and a few VERY damaging hits (almost one shots so to say). The 2 weaker npc never had a chance to do even a glancing blow there (at max incl. willpower only 1 dice).<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Environment: Like I said I overlooked that it is night and both sides would have had a mali there (aside from the vampire which was the 4th pc and possibly one of the demons). Aside from that both sides would have been hampered. Else I dont see much chance of using the environment there (pass the try of the demon player to sneak up on the enemies which he failed at though). <br /> <br /> All out attacks: nobody used them would have been possible though, but in case of the NPC they would have to have suicidal tendences to go full attack against an almost 6 feet large wolf.<br /> Surredner: the npc triedd to fly after round 4 where they took a severe beating for teh first time (being what they were they healed the glancing blows they received before). They were ripped apart.<br /> Beaten down: As the only hits not doing 1 damage were almost one hitters (5-7 damage) they were out of combat there anyway after those.<br /> <br /> Tilts: There werent enough successes rolled usually to do most tilts (also no aimed strikes at specific bodyparts else they would have had to roll chance dices without expending their willpower).<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Thus in total I'm not sure what could have been done better there (goading the enemy into all out strikes would have been an an option but the problem with that is that one of them need to spend an action to do that) and also I was surprised how ineffectual a single person with average attribute and 2 in a skill (a typical npc cop has 2 brawl as example) are. Those are almost down to chance dies without spending willpower for everry strike (against supernats they can forget it completely).<br /> <br /> The strongest dicepools on pc side were 3 dex, 3 melee + specialisation (7 dices), which also did only give a very low chance to harm the strongest enemy (quite a few hits without doing any damage at all as they were usually 2-3 successes with the knife).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:18:39-07:00","id":102748,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is, the system is designed with the expectation that the storyteller will be giving out situational bonuses and penalties with some regularity. If you just roll the dice as is, yes, you will miss a lot. What you need to do is encourage your players to do other things than &quot;I attack!&quot; *roll*. When they attempt creative tactics, reward them with bonus dice, or penalties and tilts on the mobs. For example: &quot;I grab a handful of dirt and throw it in his eyes!&quot; &quot;Ok, roll Dex + Athletics, and on a success he'll gain the Blinded tilt for a turn.&quot; Or &quot;I back him against the wall so he doesn't have as much room to try to dodge!&quot; &quot;Ok, he takes a -2 to his defense.&quot; Or &quot;I push off against the wall to try to add some extra momentum to my attack!&quot; &quot;Ok, take a +2 on your attack roll.&quot; The combat system expects you to do those kinds of things. If you don't, it will not work as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:29:00-07:00","id":102758,"title":"","content":"Ah I see. So a bit like the scion 1st edition combat system where the better the player describes and tries things the more of a bonus he gets to the roll.<br /> tnx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:35:08-07:00","id":102764,"title":"","content":"Also, don't forget that each attack reduces the target's defense by 1 against all subsequent attacks in the turn. So if everyone targets the same guy, by the last attack you should have a pretty good chance of hitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:41:13-07:00","id":102773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=102764#post102764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't forget that each attack reduces the target's defense by 1 against all subsequent attacks in the turn. So if everyone targets the same guy, by the last attack you should have a pretty good chance of hitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was already calced in.<br /> The &quot;stunting dice&quot; environment use I have to admit I hadnt considered as the core rules didnt mention things like that and in the old nwod that was unnecessary. Will try it with that rule in addition next combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T06:22:07-07:00","id":103338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=102734#post102734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surrender: the npc tried to fly after round 4 where they took a severe beating for teh first time (being what they were they healed the glancing blows they received before). They were ripped apart.</div> </div> </div> </div> What were the stated intentions of both sides in the fight?<br /> Stating Intent is probably the most important step of combat in GMC.<br /> Our first GMC combat ended before PC's first turn, as he decided he didn't really want to fight that much and surrendered to the NSC vampire's intend of \u201cbugger off and let me drink in peace\u201d. No chance to rip apart anyone, just accept the surrender condition and the fight is over. The PC got out of the situation with naught but a literal blue eye.<br /> If players regularly go for blood it will definitely increase the length of fights. Trying to really kill someone isn't easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=102734#post102734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (7 defense each with the werewolf in urshul form thus bite+2L the demon had a 4L weaponry form)</div> </div> </div> </div> Bite attack sounds like brawl focus, grappling someone and having your friends take them out is terrifyingly effective. Most werewolves will also be able to dish out quite some damage in a clinch, on top of being able to survive for a bit if a friend of your opponent gets to you first.<br /> The Demon player should think about getting two dots in Heavy weapon fighting, which would have allowed them to make mincemeat out of the opposition in short order. It's a really good investment for 2xp.<br /> With a 4L weapon a single success attack will be enough to stun most enemies if it hits the head. This means getting an area of expertise'd speciality for attacking specific body parts might also be a good investment for the Demon. Four dots in Heavy Weapons Style will allow the Demon to All-Out-Attack to their Heart's content and soak the return damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/101605-gmc-defense-and-armour-too-powerful?p=102734#post102734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The strongest dicepools on pc side were 3 dex, 3 melee + specialisation (7 dices)</div> </div> </div> </div> Those stats are pretty good for an average soldier, with some training and experience. Perfectly fine for a game focused on mortals and their interactions, allowing you to not be steamrolled by most opposition you face.<br /> For someone expecting to go into the deepest shadows of a horror setting and go tooth to claw with some of the most horrifying monsters there are they seem a bit on the low side. Werewolves are focused around fighting spirits, and the power+finesse dicepools of most spirits seem like they would make mincemeat out of such average opposition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:09:06-07:00","id":103431,"title":"","content":"If its a real medieval setting and not just a full on fantasy setting, remember armor is rare. If you fought in a battle and you weren't a noble, you didn't keep your armor. If you did, you likely sold it back.<br /> <br /> Armor really shouldn't be anymore common than it is now (The vast majority of people don't own armor). Assassins really didn't wear armor at the time, they killed and fled. Making the setting more true-to-life in a real medieval setting should cut down on most of that. Also, offense dice pool is simply 2 stats, while defense is 3 (lowest of two attributes+ath/brawl/weap). Generally defense should be lower than offensive pools, with armor being the equivalent of a weapon rather than adding to.<br /> <br /> You don't need environmental modifiers at all. You just need to be sensible in regards to how things were in period as well as not give adversaries very high athletics. Just because someone works the fields all day, doesn't mean they're adept at dodging and running. The only time your going to really see people in armor is if they're guarding a keep or in battle during a war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}